# id: BM104-clause-one-ignores-tombstones
# blinds: clause 1 knowing that a range tombstone hides a version
# covering-lane: cpp-test
# expect: killed
# control-lane: cpp-build
# expect-control: alive
#
# ON ITS OWN THIS IS ONLY OVER-KEEPING, WHICH THE CLAIM PERMITS -- and that is
# what makes it worth planting rather than obvious. It becomes a wrong answer
# only in combination with clause 2:
#
#   clause 2 drops a tombstone when nothing observable is below it;
#   that is exactly when every version beneath it is unobservable too;
#   so keeping one and dropping the other RESURRECTS the value.
#
# The two rules have to agree about what a tombstone hides, and this is the half
# that would silently stop agreeing. It is also the half the harness's own
# `Required()` has computed correctly since B3.5a -- so a divergence here is the
# engine disagreeing with the model, which is what B4 exists to catch and what
# this catches first.
